+## Trusted local runtime embedding
+
+Rust embedders of this auxiliary engine may pass
+`runtime_options.with_local_runtime(authenticated_runtime)` to
+`run_main_with_transport_options`. The bootstrap owns runtime authentication,
+lifecycle and native cleanup. App-server registers it as the actual local
+environment using the discovered environment configuration; registration failure
+aborts startup. Ordinary `AppServerRuntimeOptions` retain the default behavior.
+This capability has no JSON-RPC selector, CLI flag or network endpoint. Providers
+with controller-invisible paths remain rejected. Controller configuration loading
+retains its original sources. For injected local runtimes, `config/read` with a
+cwd reads project TOML layers through the selected provider, preserving project
+provenance and trust restrictions. Calls without a cwd retain controller settings.
+Effective feature flags use the same loaded project snapshot, managed constraints
+and runtime overrides. Provider errors are returned without controller fallback. This stage does not yet
+route thread `ConfigBuilder` or referenced instructions/agent-role files, and it
+does not confer new filesystem authorization on the provider.
+
 ## Protocol
 
 Similar to [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/), `codex app-server` supports bidirectional communication using JSON-RPC 2.0 messages (with the `"jsonrpc":"2.0"` header omitted on the wire).
diff --git a/codex-rs/app-server/src/bootstrap.rs b/codex-rs/app-server/src/bootstrap.rs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..03a54ffa9880c4fc03c199c9e12767987cf51f42
--- /dev/null
+++ b/codex-rs/app-server/src/bootstrap.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+use std::sync::Arc;
+
+use codex_exec_server::LocalRuntime;
+use codex_exec_server::ExecutorFileSystem;
+use codex_utils_path_uri::PathUri;
+
+use crate::AppServerRuntimeOptions;
+
+/// Process-local startup state supplied by a trusted app-server embedder.
+///
+/// This is a Rust bootstrap boundary, not a serialized option or a client request.
+/// Ordinary runtime options preserve the official environment discovery path.
+#[derive(Clone)]
+pub struct AppServerBootstrapOptions {
+    pub(crate) runtime_options: AppServerRuntimeOptions,
+    pub(crate) local_runtime: Option<Arc<dyn LocalRuntime>>,
+    pub(crate) host_filesystem: Option<crate::host_filesystem::HostFileSystemRoutes>,
+    pub(crate) host_process: Option<Arc<dyn crate::HostProcessBackend>>,
+    pub(crate) runtime_shutdown: tokio_util::sync::CancellationToken,
+}
+
+impl From<AppServerRuntimeOptions> for AppServerBootstrapOptions {
+    fn from(runtime_options: AppServerRuntimeOptions) -> Self {
+        Self {
+            runtime_options,
+            local_runtime: None,
+            host_filesystem: None,
+            host_process: None,
+            runtime_shutdown: tokio_util::sync::CancellationToken::new(),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+impl AppServerRuntimeOptions {
+    /// Supplies an already-authenticated runtime for the real local environment.
+    ///
+    /// The bootstrap retains authentication and native process-cleanup ownership.
+    /// Startup rejects incompatible environment configuration or unsupported path
+    /// visibility; failure never selects the ordinary controller runtime instead.
+    pub fn with_local_runtime(self, runtime: Arc<dyn LocalRuntime>) -> AppServerBootstrapOptions {
+        AppServerBootstrapOptions {
+            runtime_options: self,
+            local_runtime: Some(runtime),
+            host_filesystem: None,
+            host_process: None,
+            runtime_shutdown: tokio_util::sync::CancellationToken::new(),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+impl AppServerBootstrapOptions {
+    /// Supply a real host process owner independently of the model runtime.
+    /// This capability is installed only by bootstrap and never selected by RPC.
+    pub fn with_host_process(mut self, backend: Arc<dyn crate::HostProcessBackend>) -> std::io::Result<Self> {
+        if self.host_process.is_some() {
+            return Err(std::io::Error::new(std::io::ErrorKind::InvalidInput, "host process authority was already installed"));
+        }
+        self.host_process = Some(backend);
+        Ok(self)
+    }
+    /// Stop the server through its normal cleanup path when its native owner disappears.
+    pub fn with_runtime_shutdown(mut self, shutdown: tokio_util::sync::CancellationToken) -> Self {
+        self.runtime_shutdown = shutdown;
+        self
+    }
+    /// Supply host/UI file authority separately from the model's environment.
+    /// Roots come from trusted bootstrap. Select native W before any request;
+    /// an error from that authority never falls back to controller filesystem.
+    /// Controller roots retain the host's ordinary access and must be disjoint
+    /// from W. This routing does not sandbox unrelated host processes.
+    pub fn with_host_filesystem(mut self, workspace_root: PathUri, filesystem: Arc<dyn ExecutorFileSystem>, controller_roots: Vec<PathUri>) -> std::io::Result<Self> {
+        if self.host_filesystem.is_some() {
+            return Err(std::io::Error::new(std::io::ErrorKind::InvalidInput, "host file authority was already installed"));
+        }
+        self.host_filesystem = Some(crate::host_filesystem::HostFileSystemRoutes::new(workspace_root, filesystem, controller_roots)?);
+        Ok(self)
+    }
+}
